as quote  or there's a paraphrase but it's close  to an exact quote old  toothless aquarius and balding  a fellow by the fellow by the name of  luther  luther baldwin was sitting in a bar in  newark new jersey  when john adams and his wife abigail  came through town in their carriage and  they had  mandated that whenever they came through  a town the military had to come out and  do a 21-gun salute  and uh baldwin said to the bartender  there goes president adams they're  shooting the cannons i hope to shoot him  in the arse  and he didn't know that the bar owner  was a federalist who turned him into  john adams  john adams had him thrown in prison i  mean you know 20 newspapers were shut  down  um matthew lyon on the floor of the  house of representatives  got a fight with roger griswold the  connecticut representative  over this issue and and john adams had  him shipped off to an  unheated jail cell in for jen's vermont  for two years he ran for reelection in  the  the election of 1800 and and won his  seat back  the supreme court never intervened what  killed the alien sedition act this  insanely unconstitutional law the the  thing that created the schism  between jefferson and adams that was so  great i mean jefferson left town the day  it was signed  and literally never talked to adams in  person again  the thing that fixed that was the  election of 1800  it was the people themselves so  ultimately either  and this is what jefferson was arguing  either we believe in democracy or we  don't  if we want to try and create a  constitutional monarchy  then yeah make make the monarchs the  supreme court justices it's better than  a hereditary family  and give them final say over everything  but if you want to have an actual  constitutional  democracy then the people have to be the  ones who make the decisions  the book is out today it's called the  hidden history of the supreme court and  the betrayal of america i was lucky  enough to get an  early copy we've been speaking with the  book's author tom hartman  tom so great to have you on today thank  you david great talking with you
 

